<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Ruthenia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Red Rus', Galicia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Red Ruthenia is a historical region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/przemysl">Przemyśl</a>, in what is now south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. Once part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> and then of the principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a>, it was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-iii-the-great">Casimir III the Great</a> of Poland from 1340 and became the Ruthenian Voivodeship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a>. After 1772 it formed the core of the Austrian province of Galicia.</p></div>
